  "img": "/img-2137670.jpg",
  "excerpt": "Why hiring construction plant instead of buying keeps cash free for wages and materials on Mumbai and Maharashtra projects. A practical guide from RK.",
  "lead": "Hiring plant keeps your cash free for wages, materials and the surprises every project throws up. Instead of a large upfront payment or a fixed loan instalment, you pay for a machine only while it is working, and servicing, storage and repairs stay with the rental supplier. For most small and mid-sized contractors, that flexibility matters more than owning the machine.",
  "body": "We have been on construction sites since we were 14, and the most common way we have seen good contractors get into trouble is not bad work — it is running out of cash in the middle of a job. Plant is one of the biggest places that money gets tied up.\n\n## How does buying plant affect cashflow?\n\nWhen you buy a machine, money leaves the business on day one, or a loan instalment starts that keeps coming whether the machine works or not. Add servicing, spares, storage, transport and insurance, and the total cost of ownership goes well beyond the purchase price.\n\nNone of that is wrong if the machine is busy every week. The trouble starts when work is uneven — a delayed approval, a client who pays late, or a monsoon slowdown — and the costs keep running.\n\n## How hiring changes the picture\n\n### You pay when the machine works\nRental matches your plant cost to the job. When the phase ends, the machine goes back and the cost stops.\n\n### Your cash stays available\nMoney you don't put into a machine can pay wages on time, buy materials at the right price, or let you take on another site.\n\n### Maintenance is someone else's job\nServicing, breakdowns and spares sit with the rental supplier. At RK, machines are checked before dispatch before dispatch, and if something goes wrong you call us rather than hunting for a mechanic.\n\n### You get the right machine for each job\nDifferent phases need different plant. Hiring lets you match the machine to the work instead of making one owned machine do everything.\n\n## How to work out whether hiring helps your cashflow\n\n1. **List the machines you need** for the next few months and the weeks each one is needed.\n2. **Note your payment cycle** — when clients pay and when wages and suppliers are due.\n3. **Compare monthly cash out** for hiring versus a purchase or loan, including servicing, transport and storage.\n4. **Look at the gaps.** Any month where owning leaves you short is a month where hiring protects the job.\n5. **Review each season.** If a machine is busy almost every week, revisit buying — our 3-question rent-or-buy test helps.\n\n## When buying may still be the better call\n\nHiring is not always the answer. If one type of machine works on your own sites nearly all year, you have the cash, and you can maintain and move it, owning may cost less over time. A checked used machine can also be a sensible step. RK Enterprises does both RSP rental and RSP sale, so we can give you a fair view either way.\n\n## A Mumbai and Maharashtra angle\n\nProjects across Mumbai, Navi Mumbai and Maharashtra often run with tight schedules, staged client payments and seasonal slowdowns during the monsoon. In that setting, keeping fixed costs low and cash on hand gives you room to handle delays without stopping work.\n\n\n## Keep your cash working\n\nIf you want to free up cash on your next project, call or WhatsApp RK Enterprises. Tell us the job and the weeks, and we will suggest the right machine and the simplest way to hire it.",
